The second paragraph details the algorithms that implement the weighted edge sampling method (Algorithm 4) and how these weights are used to compute a tighter lower bound value for max regret ratio (Algorithm 5). While this is crucial information for understanding the practical application of the theory presented in Paragraph 1, it serves more as an extension or implementation detail rather than the core scientific contribution.

Therefore, based on their contributions to the main scientific content, I have assigned a higher percentage to Paragraph 1 and a lower but still significant percentage to Paragraph 2.
